-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- THE LEVEL I PEDAGOGICAL RECORD — the fields expertise can supply
--
-- The record was built with 1,616 of 1,938 entries empty, on the
-- reasoning that a teacher's knowledge comes from teaching and this
-- College has taught nobody. That was right about one kind of knowledge
-- and wrong about three others, and the conflation left the Teacher's
-- Companion, the Intervention Guide and the Differentiation Guide
-- unbuildable for a reason that did not apply to most of what they
-- would contain.
--
-- Five states now, and every entry below is one of the first three.
--
--   derived_from_curriculum  The programme states it. common_mistakes
--     and confusable_concepts are GENERATED here rather than written:
--     the self-check traps already name the confusions this lesson has
--     to catch, and the vocabulary notes already name the points at
--     which English is arbitrary. Writing them again by hand would
--     create a second version that could drift from the first.
--
--   established_pedagogy  Attested in the international teaching of
--     English, not particular to this institution.
--
--   educational_expertise  A designed judgement by the people who wrote
--     the curriculum. Defensible, improvable, and not observation.
--
-- NOTHING here is observed_in_teaching. No lesson in this programme has
-- been taught to anybody, and the fields that only a real room can fill
-- — what THIS cohort actually did, how long it actually took them, what
-- actually worked — remain not_yet_evidenced and are not listed below.
--
-- Press-drafted under delegated academic authority. Not reviewed by any
-- practising teacher.
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

-- ── Derived: the confusions the lesson's own self-check catches ──────

  value = excluded.value, evidence_state = excluded.evidence_state, source = excluded.source;

-- ── Derived: where the lesson's own vocabulary warns of arbitrariness ─

  value = excluded.value, evidence_state = excluded.evidence_state, source = excluded.source;

-- ── Established pedagogy: why these mistakes happen ──────────────────
--
-- Attested across the international teaching of English and not
-- particular to this College. Marked as synthesis, not observation.

ON CONFLICT (learning_item_id, field_key) DO UPDATE SET
  value = excluded.value, evidence_state = excluded.evidence_state, source = excluded.source;

-- ── Educational expertise: intervention, differentiation, stretch ─────
--
-- Designed by the people who wrote the curriculum. Every one of these
-- is a judgement that a teacher who runs the lesson may improve on, and
-- the state says so: this is authored guidance, not a report of what
-- worked.

ON CONFLICT (learning_item_id, field_key) DO UPDATE SET
  value = excluded.value, evidence_state = excluded.evidence_state, source = excluded.source;
